+    A mount can also be configured with a ``minimum`` and/or ``maximum`` usage
+    percentage instead of a single value. ``maximum`` behaves exactly like the
+    plain percentage shown above, firing when usage rises to or above it.
+    ``minimum`` does the opposite, firing when usage drops to or below it -
+    useful for catching a mount that is normally busy but is unexpectedly
+    almost empty, which usually means the filesystem failed to mount and the
+    path is actually backed by the root filesystem.
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                minimum: 5%
+                maximum: 90%
+
+    A mount configured this way can use ``minimum`` only, ``maximum`` only, or
+    both at once.
